 cohen  but also to help the public itself to  find out what the heck happened with  these truly beyond bizarre  circumstances of his re-imprisonment  during a time when the nation was trying  to get as many people out of prison as  possible  to help slow the spread of covid  we've still got a lot more stories to  cover i am farron cousins you can find  me on twitter facebook and instagram at  farron balanced you can also get me on  youtube at youtube.com slash fair and  balanced youtube.com slash the ring of  fire we'll be right back with more on  the david pakman show  if you value what we do at the david  pakman show remember to support us on  patreon go to patreon.com david pakman  show where you can get access to behind  the scenes videos the daily bonus show  the commercial free daily show as well  as special discounts on merch including  hats hoodies  mugs and t-shirts you can support the  show for as little as two dollars a  month check it out at patreon.com  david pakman show welcome back to the  david pakman show i am farin cousins  from ring of fire sitting in for david  pakman all of this week  let's talk about january 6th shall we  obviously in the last few weeks here  we've gotten some  very important news i would call it  about the events of that day the events  before that day the powerpoints the text  messages the emails the phone calls  all kinds of stuff  but some of the most important  information we've gotten about january 6  has actually come from the courts  late last week  the harshest sentence to date for one of  the capitol rioters was handed down the  man who assaulted a police officer with  a fire extinguisher sentenced to a  little more than five years in prison  and of course this individual expressed  his uh  sorrow his sadness  at what he did you know got the  crocodile tears going um  but  judge didn't buy it  still sentence him to more than five  years  and this is  becoming routine at this point  this is what we're seeing happening  with these judges in the sentences that  they're handing down  and here's why and this is very  important and this is something that  everybody needs to understand  about the cases these judges are hearing  because judges are telling us this past  week  that january 6 is it's not over it's not  over  and the reason for that  is because what radicalized these  individuals has not stopped it has not  gone away  while these particular people the the  ones who have been sentenced the ones  who are going to jail are currently in  jail they're probably not as likely to  engage in that kind of behavior in the  future  we're still creating another army  essentially  of these crazed people who think the  election was  stolen and that's what january 6 was  here's another thing  i filled in for david  back in august one of the stories i  talked about at the time i remember it  vividly  was the fact that judges back in august  were telling us  that we're probably facing another  january sixth type six uh situation  because of the radicalization process  because the big lie still persisted out  there  and in fact because it was being pushed  even harder in august than it was in  january  and now here we are four and a half  months after those judges told us that  more judges came out in the past week  and effectively told us the same thing  that we can expect more we can expect  worse  and we can expect this because the  radicalization still exists  because nothing has been done to stop it  because honestly it's hard to stop it  right these people have free speech we  can't tell them they're not allowed to  say these things that's illegal  but they're also not being held  accountable by the media outlets who  allow them to say these things  on their social media platforms where  they spew these lies every day in the  speeches that they give and again part  of this is because there's literally  nothing we can do about it all we can do  is go out there every day and talk about  