mation  and as somebody who does do this every  day and i'm sure david feels the same  way sometimes it feels like this  sisyphean task  we're pushing this boulder up the hill  only to watch it roll back down again  and start all over  there's no end there's no there's no  clear victory here  we're just destined to do this forever  to fight back against this conservative  misinformation  but like sisyphus himself we're never  going to stop  it's part of our job it's what we do  it's how we help  so that's what we're doing here  that's what these judges are trying to  do they're giving us the warnings  and if we don't heed these warnings  then yeah we're probably going to be  looking at something much worse than  what happened on january 6th at some  point  in the future  and speaking of january 6 as i mentioned  committees gotten their hands on all  kinds of new events  new communications new text messages new  call logs  and  they recently  got information from ali alexander  himself the man  who's a founder of stop the steel helped  organize this rally you know this was  partially at least his brainchild  and ali alexander has revealed to the  committee that yeah i had communications  with several  republican representatives who some of  them now say like oh i don't remember  ever talking to this guy  but alexander absolutely turned this  information over  to the committee  and said here it is i talked to these  people and the people of course were uh  representative paul gosar a text  exchange with representative mo brooks  and uh also  andy biggs of arizona although he says  he did not  actually talk to him on the phone that  was more of an in-person thing  pretty interesting right so how do we  know aly alexander has given the  committee everything he has  well because that is actually what  alexander is charging in a new lawsuit  because the committee still says we want  your records we want all your records  you you've given us a lot right you know  we asked 